-- title:
--   Actual admissible original Lévy finite-band signed L1 limit from source derivative bounds
-- statement:
--   For a sequence of original stopped predictable compact reserve bands whose concrete Lévy jump compensation and generator drifts coincide source-exactly with Mmesh and Bmesh, derive L1-centred and nonpositive signed expectations of their almost-everywhere limits. Each finite-band source integrability and moment sign follows from the proved admissible HJB drift theorem and original compensator. Convergence and integrable dominators remain explicit because they require separate uniform-integrability proof.
-- source:
--   Depends on new P3-E2 source-admissible signed compensation and established 943efd39 dominated signed mesh limit.

